    {
      "id": "KzBjqBNq4KujpU8V2xkgk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 1754.4984130859375,
      "width": 750,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLi",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1350686857,
      "version": 843,
      "versionNonce": 1728773609,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1742715865864,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "U-net architecture is commonly used to achieve the denoising of images with\nnoise to obtain images similar to the ones in the training dataset. \nFrom the noise input image, we go through layers which finally yield an\nestimate of the error which was added for time steps t to obtain the noisy\nimage from the original image. the training loss is the difference between the\nobtained noise and the actual noise which was added unto time steps t",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "U-net architecture is commonly used to achieve the denoising of images with noise to obtain images similar to the ones in the training dataset. \nFrom the noise input image, we go through layers which finally yield an estimate of the error which was added for time steps t to obtain the noisy  image from the original image. the training loss is the difference between the obtained noise and the actual noise which was added unto time steps t",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "F8yt5KWnChX7XIV_VIKxi",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 462,
      "y": 1950.4984130859375,
      "width": 683,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1282911977,
      "version": 310,
      "versionNonce": 1637533863,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1742715717641,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "now to generate images based on captions, we need to do conditional\nimage generation, which takes the prompts and pushes the neural\nnetwork to generate images according to the prompt from the noisy\nimage.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "now to generate images based on captions, we need to do conditional image generation, which takes the prompts and pushes the neural network to generate images according to the prompt from the noisy image.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "vpTPzBjNDl7Uc9aEoovrM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 458,
      "y": 2094.4984130859375,
      "width": 628,
      "height": 200,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLk",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1274107817,
      "version": 519,
      "versionNonce": 495205001,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1742715962578,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "classifier free guidance : \nin this approach, we combine the noisy image and condition i.e\nthe prompt to obtain the estimate of the noise. with some\nprobability we zero out the condition getting the output from\nthe noise alone. we take a weighted sum of both of these\noutputs to allow the network to decide how much of attention\nto pay to the image generation process and how much to the\nprompt condition signal",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "classifier free guidance : \nin this approach, we combine the noisy image and condition i.e the prompt to obtain the estimate of the noise. with some probability we zero out the condition getting the output from the noise alone. we take a weighted sum of both of these outputs to allow the network to decide how much of attention to pay to the image generation process and how much to the prompt condition signal",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "hRZNWIBxmfTBKJazHGcjP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 527,
      "y": 2353.4984130859375,
      "width": 776,
      "height": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLl",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1786873065,
      "version": 354,
      "versionNonce": 1605394279,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1742733088762,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "in stable diffusion, instead of working on the full images, we learn a latent\nrepresentation of the image using Variational auto encoder and then perform\nthe diffusion forward and reverse on these latent spaces and retrieve back\nthe image. ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "in stable diffusion, instead of working on the full images, we learn a latent representation of the image using Variational auto encoder and then perform the diffusion forward and reverse on these latent spaces and retrieve back the image. ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
